      "result": "\n\nWritten to `submission/main.c`. The demo works as follows:\n\n- `low_prio_thread` (prio 10) starts, takes `pi_mutex`, prints \"Low: holding mutex\", sleeps 300 ms, then releases.\n- `med_prio_thread` (prio 7) wakes at 50 ms and loops, printing that it cannot preempt the boosted low-priority holder.\n- `high_prio_thread` (prio 4) wakes at 100 ms and blocks on `k_mutex_lock(&pi_mutex, K_FOREVER)` — this is what boosts the low-priority holder to priority 4 via priority inheritance, so the medium thread (7) cannot preempt it. At 300 ms the low thread releases, high acquires, prints \"High: acquired mutex\", and unlocks.\n- `main()` just idles with `k_sleep(K_FOREVER)` since `K_THREAD_DEFINE` threads start automatically.",
